# std/rustc (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): the worker factory is part of the
# irreducible SEEDED core — it can't be built by the machinery it IS (rustc
# compiling rustc is a cycle), so like flake-builder it names a sentinel image
# and the core-seeder-runner answers with the pre-built result. The sentinel is
# distinct (`docker://seeded-rustc`) so rustc's key can't collide with another
# minimal-entry core item's. bootstrap hand-builds the result —
# curry(runner, worker1=<worker-rustc binary>, cargo=<cargo image>, worker-common)
# — and seeds it under this expression's arg-tree key. Nothing is staged into
# the checked-in entry: a consumer fetching this tree gets a resolvable
# expression, and the binary rides in the seed, not here.
run --base:docker=seeded-rustc --in:@=.
